# The only binary package here with no indi-stable-3rdparty-libs-<vendor>
# Depends, because eqmod has no vendor blob behind it -- it talks the
# Skywatcher serial/network protocol directly. libnova and libgsl arrive
# through ${shlibs:Depends} on their own, both being ordinary distribution
# packages that ship real shlibs files.
Package: indi-stable-3rdparty-drivers-eqmod
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, indi-stable-core-libs
Description: EQMod / Skywatcher-protocol mount INDI drivers
 indi_eqmod_telescope, indi_azgti_telescope,
 indi_staradventurergti_telescope and indi_staradventurer2i_telescope --
 four binaries, not one, sharing skywatcher.cpp's motor-control code:
 EQMod-protocol Skywatcher mounts (including the Wave 100i/150i), the AZ-GTi
 in equatorial WiFi mode, and both Star Adventurer GTi and 2i variants.
 .
 Needs no vendor SDK, so unlike every other package here it depends only on
 indi-stable-core-libs. Does not include indi_ahpgt_telescope, which
 upstream gates behind an option that is off by default.
 .
 This is an unofficial third-party build. It is not affiliated with or
 endorsed by the INDI project.

# Like eqmod, neither of these has a vendor blob and so neither carries an
# indi-stable-3rdparty-libs Depends. Unlike eqmod they need nothing beyond
# INDI itself -- no libnova, no libgsl -- so they added no build dependency
# at all. Both are LGPL-2.1-or-later, read from every .cpp/.h header in both
# directories rather than spot-checked; see debian/copyright.
Package: indi-stable-3rdparty-drivers-armadillo-platypus
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, indi-stable-core-libs
Description: Lunatico Armadillo, Platypus, Dragonfly, Seletek and Beaver INDI drivers
 Six binaries from one source directory, for Lunatico Astronomia's
 controller family: indi_armadillo_focus and indi_platypus_focus (focusers),
 indi_seletek_rotator (rotator), indi_dragonfly and indi_dragonfly_dome
 (relay controller and its dome front-end) and indi_beaver_dome.
 .
 The first package in this source package to ship a udev rule. It is
 installed under a namespaced filename so it takes effect without colliding
 with a distribution rule for the same hardware.
 .
 Its catalogue is indi_lunatico.xml, named for the vendor rather than for
 the source directory or any binary in it.
 .
 This is an unofficial third-party build. It is not affiliated with or
 endorsed by the INDI project.

Package: indi-stable-3rdparty-drivers-maxdomeii
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, indi-stable-core-libs
Description: MaxDome II observatory dome INDI driver
 indi_maxdomeii, for the MaxDome II dome controller. Needs no vendor SDK and
 no library beyond INDI itself.
 .
 Does not include test-maxdomeii, an upstream standalone test harness that
 the default build compiles but never installs.
 .
 This is an unofficial third-party build. It is not affiliated with or
 endorsed by the INDI project.

# Three more non-blob drivers. They link libnova, and celestronaux also
# libgsl, both already build dependencies here since eqmod -- so this slice
# added none. All three are LGPL-2.1-or-later; see debian/copyright.
Package: indi-stable-3rdparty-drivers-aok
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, indi-stable-core-libs
Description: Astro-Electronic AOK Skywalker mount INDI driver
 indi_lx200aok, an LX200-protocol driver for AOK Skywalker mount
 controllers.
 .
 The source directory is indi-aok, the upstream build option is
 WITH_SKYWALKER, the binary is indi_lx200aok and the catalogue is
 indi_aok.xml. None of those can be derived from the others.
 .
 This is an unofficial third-party build. It is not affiliated with or
 endorsed by the INDI project.

Package: indi-stable-3rdparty-drivers-avalon
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, indi-stable-core-libs
Description: Avalon StarGo mount INDI driver
 indi_lx200stargo, an LX200-protocol driver for Avalon Instruments StarGo
 mount controllers. Its catalogue is indi_avalon.xml, named for the vendor
 rather than the binary.
 .
 This is an unofficial third-party build. It is not affiliated with or
 endorsed by the INDI project.

Package: indi-stable-3rdparty-drivers-celestronaux
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, indi-stable-core-libs
Description: Celestron AUX-protocol mount INDI driver
 indi_celestron_aux, speaking Celestron's AUX protocol directly rather than
 the NexStar serial protocol the core INDI driver uses. The only driver
 here that needs libgsl as well as libnova.
 .
 This is an unofficial third-party build. It is not affiliated with or
 endorsed by the INDI project.

Package: indi-stable-3rdparty-drivers-touptek
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, indi-stable-core-libs,
         indi-stable-3rdparty-libs-touptek (= 2.2.4.1-1)
